This directory is deliberately NOT under the AGPL that covers the rest of the
repository. A specification has to be implementable without infecting the
implementation; the reasoning is in ../LICENSING.md.

Two licences apply here, by kind of file:

  Apache-2.0            everything that is executed or parsed
    schema/*.json         the JSON Schemas
    vocabulary/*.json     the closed read and action vocabularies
    example/**            the worked example manifest and its solutions
    example-desktop/**    the second worked example: a project that repairs
                          software it did not write
    monitor/verify_log.py the reference log monitor
                        Full text: LICENSE-APACHE-2.0

  CC-BY-4.0             the prose
    SPEC.md
    INTEGRATING.md
                        Full text: LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0

Neither licence grants any right in the name PODSHL. Apache-2.0 says so in
section 6; CC-BY-4.0 grants copyright and neighbouring rights and nothing
else. Fork this freely. Do not present a fork as the operator.
